  THE VERDICT — the registered primary cell

    d' POOLED over B   (registered)       1.1199 +- 0.0642   -> accuracy 0.7122
    d' WITHIN B        (addendum)         1.2643 +- 0.0583   -> accuracy 0.7364
    d' drive RATIO     (EXCLUDED)         4.6016 +- 0.1366   -> accuracy 0.9893

    THE DRIVE RATIO IS EXCLUDED, AND THE REASON IS ALGEBRA RATHER THAN
    ITS VALUE. J = 1 - rec . T/S, so the mean difference AND the SD both
    scale linearly in `rec` and it CANCELS EXACTLY: the statistic is
    scale-free, its d' does not depend on the gap or on tau_rec, and its
    gap ladder is FLAT. It therefore predicts near-perfect accuracy at a
    5000 ms gap, where §63 measured the trace already dead. An estimator
    whose normalisation divides out the very quantity under test cannot
    model a physical readout. `rank-one-noise-saturates-the-estimator` in
    a new costume: what is missing is a noise term that does NOT scale
    with the signal, which both kept statistics have and this one does not.

    LABEL-DESTROYED, pooled               0.0152 +- 0.0030
    LABEL-DESTROYED, within-B             0.0788 +- 0.0142
